text:
Alright, I can help you with that. We'll swap the times for your "Book" and "Reading & Labs (Core Engineering)" blocks on Tuesday.

Since neither of these blocks is currently linked to a goal, I'll also propose creating a 'Learning & Development' goal. This way, any time you log against these activities will contribute to your progress, which aligns with your "why" of growing as an engineer.

Here's the plan: First, we'll create the 'Learning & Development' goal. Then, we'll update the 'Reading & Labs' block to take the 'Book' time slot, and the 'Book' block to take the 'Reading & Labs' time slot, linking both to your new goal.

```coach-proposal
{
  "summary": "Swap Tuesday's 'Book' and 'Reading & Labs' blocks, and create a 'Learning & Development' goal to link them.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "type": "CREATE_GOAL",
      "payload": {
        "title": "Learning & Development",
        "category": "LEARNING",
        "targetHours": 120,
        "description": "Dedicate time to structured learning, reading, and labs to grow as an engineer.",
        "deadline": "2027-02-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "UPDATE_SCHEDULE_BLOCK",
      "id": "1a78bae8-7aac-4d57-abe1-53f3aa8ede25",
      "expectedTitle": "Reading & Labs (Core Engineering)",
      "payload": {
        "startTime": "09:00",
        "endTime": "11:00",
        "goalId": "$ref:0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "UPDATE_SCHEDULE_BLOCK",
      "id": "8d8947e7-5ec5-4d64-aed7-4507dd3f6b09",
      "expectedTitle": "Book",
      "payload": {
        "startTime": "07:00",
        "endTime": "09:00",
        "goalId": "$ref:0"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

This will move your "Reading & Labs (Core Engineering)" block to Tuesday from 9:00 AM to 11:00 AM, and your "Book" block to Tuesday from 7:00 AM to 9:00 AM, both linked to your new learning goal.

Many of your other schedule blocks, such as "Family Time" and "Work", are also not currently linked to any goals, meaning the time you spend on them isn't being tracked. Would you like to create a goal for your "Family Time" blocks next?
